      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of absolute sovereignty is often undermined by the reality of international security threats, especially when those threats are inherently destabilizing to the global system. When an authoritarian regime actively plans to destabilize neighboring democracies or spread its ideology through coercion, its claim to absolute sovereignty becomes a shield for aggression. Therefore, the defense of core human rights and democratic principles supersedes the abstract notion of unchecked sovereignty.",
      "source": "target",
