      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The determination of \"destabilizing\" regimes is not a matter of convenience, but of objective threat assessment against established international norms, which are themselves codified by democratic consensus. To suggest that only certain governments are \"real\" is a cynical misreading; we are asserting that governments that systematically deny basic human dignity are illegitimate in the eyes of the international community. If we allow might to make right without moral restraint, then the entire concept of international law collapses into pure anarchy, which is a far greater danger than necessary intervention.",
